    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 62 tests pass (green build). The change is complete.\n\n## What I implemented\n\nThe requirement: `POST /api/owners` may carry an `Idempotency-Key` header; a repeated create with an already-seen key returns the originally created owner with **200** instead of creating a duplicate.\n\nSince this project routes REST through OfficeFloor function pipelines (not `@RestController`), I wired it as pipeline steps + an escalation, following the conventions in `AGENTS.md`:\n\n**New pieces**\n- `rest/support/IdempotencyStore.java` \u2014 a `@Component` singleton mapping key \u2192 created owner id (`ConcurrentHashMap`, first-writer-wins), shared across requests.\n- `rest/function/owner/CheckIdempotencyKey.java` \u2014 new **first** step. Reads the header via `ServerHttpConnection`, publishes the key as an `Out<String>` variable for later, and if the key was already seen loads that owner and throws `IdempotentCreateReplayException` to short-circuit the whole create pipeline.\n- `rest/escalation/IdempotentCreateReplayException.java` (checked) + `IdempotentCreateReplayHandler.java` \u2014 the handler maps the carried owner and responds `200`. (Owner\u2192Pet is `FetchType.EAGER`, so mapping the detached owner outside governance is safe.)\n- `rest/function/owner/RecordIdempotencyKey.java` \u2014 new step after `save`, records key \u2192 new owner id (no-op when no key was present).\n\n**Wiring**\n- `owners.POST.yml`: inserted `checkIdempotency` before `validate`, and `recordIdempotency` between `countHousehold` and `respond`, both under the existing `transaction` governance.\n- Added `officefloor/escalation/\u2026IdempotentCreateReplayException.yml`.\n\nPlacing the check *before* body validation keeps the \"read the body only once\" rule intact \u2014 a replay never binds `@RequestBody`; only the create path does. A key whose owner has since disappeared falls through and creates anew.",
