    "probe_text": "I now have the complete picture. Here is the ordered list of everything applied to `POST /api/owners`.\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`. Without the `OWNER_ADMIN` role the whole endpoint is rejected before any function runs.\n\nThe whole pipeline runs under a single `transaction` governance, so all writes commit once at the end (or roll back together on any escalation).\n\n## Ordered pipeline\n\n**1. `CheckIdempotencyKey`** \u2014 *side-effect + short-circuit.* Reads the optional `Idempotency-Key` header (blank treated as absent), publishes it for later. If the key was already used to create an owner **and** that owner still exists, throws `IdempotentCreateReplayException` \u2192 returns the existing owner (200), skipping creation entirely.\n\n**2. `ValidateOwnerFields`** \u2014 *validation.* First runs bean validation via `@Valid` on `OwnerFieldsDto` (pattern/size constraints, e.g. postcode `^[0-9]{4}$`). Then rejects with `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (400, naming each field) if any of **firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone** is null/blank \u2014 catching whitespace-only values. Address is satisfied by either `addressLine1` (structured) or flat `address`, checked in normalized form. Publishes the validated body.\n\n**3. `CheckRegistrationDateNotFuture`** \u2014 *validation.* If a `registrationDate` was supplied and is after the server date, throws `FutureRegistrationDateException` (400). Checked against the raw supplied date, before any weekend roll.\n\n**4. `ValidatePostcode`** \u2014 *validation.* Postcode optional. When present (already `^[0-9]{4}$`), if the city maps to a known region the 4 digits must fall in that region's range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099); otherwise `InvalidPostcodeException` (400). Unknown-region cities accept any 4-digit code.\n\n**5. `NormalizeOwnerTelephone`** \u2014 *side-effect + validation.* Rewrites telephone to E.164 (keeps `+`/country code, else assumes `+61` and drops a leading `0`, strips spaces/dashes/brackets). If the result isn't a valid E.164 (8\u201315 digits), throws `InvalidTelephoneException` (400). Mutates the body in place.\n\n**6. `NormalizeOwnerEmail`** \u2014 *side-effect + validation.* Email optional: null/blank set to null. When present, must match the email regex or `InvalidEmailException` (400); valid value stored lower-cased on the body.\n\n**7. `CheckEmailDomainAllowed`** \u2014 *validation.* If the (present) email's domain is on the disposable blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`), throws `DisposableEmailDomainException` (400).\n\n**8. `NormalizeOwnerAddress`** \u2014 *side-effect.* Normalizes the address to canonical form. Structured form preferred: normalizes `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` and composes the flat `address`; otherwise normalizes flat `address` alone. Mutates the body in place so all later steps see the normalized address.\n\n**9. `CheckOwnerCityCapacity`** \u2014 *validation.* Counts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive, trimmed). If \u2265 **50**, throws `CityAtCapacityException` (409).\n\n**10. `CheckOwnerDailyLimit`** \u2014 *validation.* Counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals this request's effective business day (supplied-or-today, rolled off weekends). If \u2265 **100**, throws `DailyOwnerLimitException` (429).\n\n**11. `BuildOwner`** \u2014 *side-effect.* Maps the DTO to an `Owner` entity and sets `registrationDate` to the effective business day (weekend \u2192 next Monday). Publishes the built entity.\n\n**12. `CountNamesakes`** \u2014 *side-effect.* Sets `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners sharing first+last name (case-insensitive, trimmed); excludes the new owner.\n\n**13. `AssignCustomerCode`** \u2014 *side-effect.* Sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode/city via `Locality`, else `UNKNOWN`; HASH8 = first 8 upper-hex of SHA-256 over `telephone + lastName`). On collision with an existing code, appends `-<n>` (smallest n \u2265 2) to de-duplicate.\n\n**14. `AssignMembershipNumber`** \u2014 *side-effect.* Sets `membershipNumber` = `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, YY = last two digits of the fiscal year of the registration date.\n\n**15. `AssignHousehold`** \u2014 *side-effect.* Sets `householdId` = first 12 hex of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode` (deterministic; shared by same last-name+postcode owners).\n\n**16. `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique`** \u2014 *validation.* Scanning non-soft-deleted owners: (a) if the derived `identityKey` (`telephone|email|householdId`) exactly matches an existing owner \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (409), always; (b) if an existing owner shares the `householdId` \u2192 409, **unless** the request set `sharesHousehold` (admits as declared member).\n\n**17. `CheckPossibleDuplicate`** \u2014 *side-effect.* Among non-deleted owners, finds one with same last name + same postcode but **different** telephone and **different** householdId. Sets `possibleDuplicate` = whether any matched, and `possibleDuplicateOf` = lowest matching id (else absent). Does not reject.\n\n**18. `SaveOwner`** \u2014 *side-effect.* Persists the owner via the repository (assigns the id).\n\n**19. `AuditOwnerCreated`** \u2014 *side-effect.* Emits an `AUDIT` log line with the new id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel, membershipNumber.\n\n**20. `MarkBulkSignupWarning`** \u2014 *side-effect.* Sets `bulkSignupWarning` = true if more than **80** owners already registered on the current business day (read-time flag on the DTO).\n\n**21. `CountHouseholdMembers`** \u2014 *side-effect.* Sets `householdSize` = count of owners sharing the `householdId` (self included; 1 if no householdId).\n\n**22. `RecordIdempotencyKey`** \u2014 *side-effect.* If the request carried an idempotency key and the owner has an id, stores key\u2192id (first write wins) so future replays return this owner.\n\n**23. `RespondWithOwnerCreated`** \u2014 *side-effect.* Maps the owner to `OwnerDto` and responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n---\n\n### Summary\n\n- **Rejections (validations), in order:** authorization \u2192 bean `@Valid` \u2192 required fields \u2192 future registration date \u2192 postcode/region \u2192 telephone E.164 \u2192 email syntax \u2192 disposable email domain \u2192 city capacity (409) \u2192 daily limit (429) \u2192 identity/household duplicate (409). Plus the idempotency-replay short-circuit at the very top.\n- **Mutations before save:** telephone, email, address normalization; then `registrationDate`, `namesakeCount`, `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, `householdId`, `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf`.\n- **After save:** id assignment, audit log, `bulkSignupWarning`, `householdSize`, idempotency-key record, then the 201 response.\n\nOne thing worth flagging: several checks (city capacity, daily limit, namesakes, customer-code collision, identity/household duplicate) each call `ownerRepository.findAll()` and scan all owners in memory \u2014 that's O(owners) per step, so this create path does a lot of full-table scans."
